#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161704 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5b58f4ff-b6ed-5df6-b04f-137e285d5460" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Linear Form"}] :question/id #uuid "59ea7ebb-5b69-5551-a5b9-c286e2730881" :question/math-academy-id "e-8160" :question/problem "The linear form $f(\\mathbf{x})$ is defined as $f(\\mathbf{x}) = \\mathbf{a} \\mathbf{x},$ where ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/assets/e104f037293e19fe2a12d9b2e14cc344d5cca06f933f393755cf03568b5702c0.png)  Evaluate the function when ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/assets/8832f5ec6073de4098b3b0f856a3ab5e000926a9d09f76e87909adb67777cc17.png)" :question/worked-solution "Substituting ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/assets/4c5ce198c2271b51807f4c17fffdf4288c524ff73469196bd481dc489c5a0e40.png) we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =ax \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-5)+0\\cdot 8+4\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =-15+0+20 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161705 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7083d465-9871-59ca-97fa-583e740e961f" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Bilinear Form"}] :question/id #uuid "30204c69-3362-5cc1-a04a-3bb83559b300" :question/math-academy-id "e-8161" :question/problem "Consider the the bilinear form $B(\\mathbf{x},\\mathbf{y}),$ given by \n\n$$\nB(\\mathbf{x},\\mathbf{y})= 2 x_1y_2 - x_2y_2 +3 x_2y_3-x_3y_1\n$$\n\n \n\nEvaluate $B(\\mathbf{x},\\mathbf{y})$ when ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/assets/dcea1a36972408a1f6a56577f61150bd8e4c2b91284820ca47c632a985d912ca.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/assets/f9885ea740945a64e44931aca4befbd4022a84ae0fa1454627f2b44133eb4651.png)" :question/worked-solution "We are given that \n\n$\\qquad$ ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/assets/652258046237288de7102e402a266dd3afff1abfecf97aa2156a351a7611afb3.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/assets/58ef5fbadaf595035dc902aac9b66bbce61fea79b6a4144ed060f0486dda982c.png) \n\nSubstituting these into the bilinear expression, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & =2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{3}-{x}_{3}{y}_{1} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 1\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 2+3\\cdot 1\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =4-2+3-2 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161706 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55277d69-eedc-5c5c-883a-083746e00947" :knowledge-point/title "Writing Down a Bilinear Form Given Its Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "34398117-07f4-51d9-a879-30a0f6891e68" :question/math-academy-id "e-8162" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/assets/4dfdcd2e2f0d80ee8b6633b0dd4bc33b477b22e4db0f2ad36cbfa62eef702659.png)\nConsider the matrix ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/assets/15fa693fff5bc0eb2a8851089612b5a3fb969c3fd5fbc7c0821e58e52ff4260d.png) above.  Write down a bilinear form ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/assets/7c7f59284956b7a02d9d9d16387cfba529479fb49aa8efff3bfa908be0fbb04f.png) in terms of the components of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/assets/ed54028979894fad0ac2b928c90c9eeea9361d1c8514fb61ee8ce28435ac2a5c.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/assets/9849708035aaa18397dfafbbcdfeb923f576296406c494c30093477f6b2aaa33.png)" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/assets/e8f54943816e5af3ad7a3b92ff68887d8126962ffcba1d3109d10390616d8a04.png) of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/assets/3397629141c3034fbd4b5cd5bd8c554676175a4b1e3f5eccd26cc5d66ee1bec8.png) corresponds to the term ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/assets/e4b6d1207e1c34e37c760af85eb4a4e5594e3db2da2c4ba4841a4106de188c1b.png) in the expression of the bilinear form:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/assets/734889027df1469d75a4506f295a277b908081224b5860ebf9ec8ea432053dd9.png)\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a bilinear form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/assets/4ccd64cd17dd595c826e5a8bf13d4bf991c57d128d7a3fbca5a49eaf265f0867.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161707 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f60cd05d-e4af-5bf1-8827-cab48da934f1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Bilinear Form"}] :question/id #uuid "84e1b597-45d7-51f4-aaa9-8a52c753a510" :question/math-academy-id "e-8163" :question/problem "The matrix of the bilinear form $B(\\mathbf{x},\\mathbf{y}) = 2x_1y_1 + 2x_2y_1 - x_3 y_2+2x_3y_3$ is given below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & 0 & 0 \\\\ b & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & c & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Each term $a_{ij}x_i y_j$ in the expression of the bilinear form corresponds to the entry $a_{ij}$ of the matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & =2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}-{x}_{3}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{3}{y}_{3} \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+0{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+0{x}_{1}{y}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+0{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+0{x}_{2}{y}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,0{x}_{3}{y}_{1}+(-1){x}_{3}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{3}{y}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, the corresponding matrix of the bilinear form is\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/assets/24b1e29dccdff51c2ca2c7780a8a5dfcf9c74ed91d48afdde8a14c5127f89ce1.png)\n\nTherefore, $a=2,$ $b=2,$ and $c=-1.$ Finally, \n\n$$\na+b+c=2+2+(-1) = 3.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186324943 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5b58f4ff-b6ed-5df6-b04f-137e285d5460" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Linear Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d774ccb2-55a3-51c4-b063-5c1ce6c59b89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324945} {:answer/id #uuid "b55c4d70-fcb9-51d5-8580-67966effce3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324946} {:answer/id #uuid "78284014-2038-500e-8bde-0d780e7975b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324947} {:answer/id #uuid "8d133599-1d18-53f9-81f1-5843a1cbcbb2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324948} {:answer/id #uuid "b69b5661-1577-58ff-be35-646e21903453" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324949}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d774ccb2-55a3-51c4-b063-5c1ce6c59b89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324945} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b204740-ab27-57d6-9100-2e78a25c8998" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324944}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6f7eba9d-d05c-525c-ab4e-f81697290353" :question/math-academy-id "q-140851" :question/problem "The linear form $f(x)$ is defined as $f(x)=ax,$ where $a=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}].$  Evaluate the function when $x=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Substituting $x=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =ax \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-2)+(-1)\\cdot 5+2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-6-5+4 \\\\  & =-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186324950 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5b58f4ff-b6ed-5df6-b04f-137e285d5460" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Linear Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b5cb4ff2-b59e-5109-a007-c1ad4a9bb72c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324952} {:answer/id #uuid "52dc4825-e7e3-5f34-a549-00668cf6ccfd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324953} {:answer/id #uuid "4c6f2426-c339-5b6e-97d7-03a0f4599db2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324954} {:answer/id #uuid "cf495cf6-ed91-561b-bc05-13913bce9edc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324955} {:answer/id #uuid "6d6db5e0-bcaf-53bc-b36d-3b0a16417c6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324956}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "52dc4825-e7e3-5f34-a549-00668cf6ccfd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324953} :answer-field/id #uuid "ffbc68a7-7136-5c72-b84d-b304b5d47ebd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324951}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1f422414-9bb3-5223-a7d4-4ef5614150c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-140852" :question/problem "The linear form $f(x)$ is defined as $f(x)=ax,$ where $a=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 & 4\\end{aligned}].$  Evaluate the function when $x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Substituting $x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =ax \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =3\\cdot 1+(-6)\\cdot 2+4\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =3-12+20 \\\\  & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186324957 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7083d465-9871-59ca-97fa-583e740e961f" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Bilinear Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "963f02b5-d3bd-5344-b3ea-46d180eb2a47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "70" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324959} {:answer/id #uuid "34aabec3-dd72-5a5d-8be9-1fe90dd43eef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "65" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324960} {:answer/id #uuid "6fad0955-2c77-5a27-ace9-313faa5547eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324961} {:answer/id #uuid "f9a60985-a1a8-58de-9c9d-b14d7496c908" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324962} {:answer/id #uuid "bba4077f-418a-5b81-abf5-5024ef239a47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "105" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324963}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "34aabec3-dd72-5a5d-8be9-1fe90dd43eef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "65" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324960} :answer-field/id #uuid "af01d3b4-c01b-50b8-95a0-fad12d51638d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324958}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1e3b7ee0-32f5-5673-83e7-92ec6cfd0c0e" :question/math-academy-id "q-140861" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nGiven the matrix $A$ above, evaluate the bilinear form $B(x,y)={x}^{T}\\,Ay$ when $x=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Substituting $x=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & ={x}^{T}\\,Ay \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 20\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =65.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186324964 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55277d69-eedc-5c5c-883a-083746e00947" :knowledge-point/title "Writing Down a Bilinear Form Given Its Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cb5104cb-d1ad-52df-a6f8-7deaa56b6653" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{1}{y}_{1}-3{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324966} {:answer/id #uuid "e6272424-adf3-5b71-b1c2-56d575e0324a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-3{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324967} {:answer/id #uuid "e27e2605-5c20-5fc6-87e2-8c0418e0ad74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}-3{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324968} {:answer/id #uuid "7dfc8ed5-fc56-5168-8fa5-6b057bf79db8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-3{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324969} {:answer/id #uuid "69c06591-8c13-5abb-a691-7d1577382dd8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324970}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e27e2605-5c20-5fc6-87e2-8c0418e0ad74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}-3{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324968} :answer-field/id #uuid "5036ef38-8726-5fc8-9453-2753ce2dc7ff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324965}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a9f93327-9194-5e9f-a2c9-bc612bf1c0ad" :question/math-academy-id "q-140863" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & \\,\\,-3 \\\\ \\,\\,3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following represents the corresponding bilinear form ${x}^{T}\\,Ay$ in terms of the components of $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ${a}_{ij}$ of $A$ corresponds to the term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{y}_{j}$ in the expression of the bilinear form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ay & =2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+(-3){x}_{1}{y}_{2}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+1{x}_{2}{y}_{2} \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}-3{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+{x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a bilinear form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ay & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & \\,\\,-3 \\\\ \\,\\,3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2{y}_{1}-3{y}_{2} \\\\ 3{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{1}(2{y}_{1}-3{y}_{2})+{x}_{2}(3{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}) \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}-3{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+{x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186324971 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5b58f4ff-b6ed-5df6-b04f-137e285d5460" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Linear Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e1ca92f-f060-50dd-8303-5773b5286f55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324973} {:answer/id #uuid "c450a127-bfaf-598b-b646-2b322c613e42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324974} {:answer/id #uuid "5cb63bdf-b179-5e30-a771-e1280dba75d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324975} {:answer/id #uuid "db225d79-b864-56c5-8074-2959e9510202" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324976} {:answer/id #uuid "e74c446f-5699-5a89-9812-205e0d7db660" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324977}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5cb63bdf-b179-5e30-a771-e1280dba75d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324975} :answer-field/id #uuid "276511d3-dab4-5280-a452-b9eee94ebb9f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324972}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a14c9b26-9e8f-5fa1-86e3-aef4ea62723d" :question/math-academy-id "q-93900" :question/problem "The linear form $f(x)$ is defined as $f(x)=ax,$ where $a=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1\\end{aligned}].$   Evaluate the function when $x=[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Substituting $x=[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}],$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =ax \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot (-6)+1\\cdot (-8) \\\\  & =12-8 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186324978 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7083d465-9871-59ca-97fa-583e740e961f" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Bilinear Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a4486117-a0b3-5ca3-83bf-9cc5af3e4c15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324980} {:answer/id #uuid "25611bbb-85c8-5465-83a4-c98126065f55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324981} {:answer/id #uuid "385ed354-6954-5c24-9628-9dcf52e408d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324982} {:answer/id #uuid "8f649494-8251-5504-9382-0284291bdb57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324983} {:answer/id #uuid "99e92b1e-96ab-5e53-b6ed-187d3af47196" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324984}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a4486117-a0b3-5ca3-83bf-9cc5af3e4c15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324980} :answer-field/id #uuid "19c0c8c0-09bf-5a27-9537-224d4ba1845c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324979}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b1017db8-9e30-5331-81ba-2a235c100c98" :question/math-academy-id "q-93916" :question/problem "Consider the bilinear form $B(x,y),$ given by \n\n$$\nB(x,y)={x}_{1}{y}_{1}+{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+{x}_{2}{y}_{2}.\n$$\n\n \n\nEvaluate $B(x,y)$ when $x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "We are given that \n\n$\\,$ $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,y=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSubstituting these into the bilinear expression, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & ={x}_{1}{y}_{1}+{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+{x}_{2}{y}_{2} \\\\  & =1\\cdot 3+1\\cdot 3+2\\cdot 1\\cdot (-1)+1\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =3+3-2-1 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186324985 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5b58f4ff-b6ed-5df6-b04f-137e285d5460" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Linear Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d866fc8b-e9ea-5608-a5ee-84608c8aff79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324987} {:answer/id #uuid "29357b8d-9c0f-55d6-804c-1d6f7f357c45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324988} {:answer/id #uuid "71865530-d862-5d6a-b060-ff0194ec3d31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324989} {:answer/id #uuid "c94c1007-b263-57d9-b754-43cc62fd0efe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324990} {:answer/id #uuid "b4ca4666-1e3e-5129-aceb-ea79453dd4bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324991}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29357b8d-9c0f-55d6-804c-1d6f7f357c45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324988} :answer-field/id #uuid "3853306d-1129-54b1-86a8-ce2b8d117a21" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324986}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d0aba727-cdff-536a-b0e0-bcfbe8ec783e" :question/math-academy-id "q-93968" :question/problem "The linear form $f(x)$ is defined as $f(x)=ax,$ where $a=[\\begin{aligned}6 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].$  Evaluate the function when $x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Substituting $x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}],$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =ax \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =6\\cdot 3+(-1)\\cdot 8+1\\cdot (-7) \\\\  & =18-8-7 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186324992 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5b58f4ff-b6ed-5df6-b04f-137e285d5460" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Linear Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "efaa1029-3db2-5cc9-b5bb-5ce5f9e7d75d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324994} {:answer/id #uuid "7bed994b-775c-565b-b3f2-4a6984304f38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324995} {:answer/id #uuid "59d1261f-409d-5ebf-bf5c-e8bada99d6a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324996} {:answer/id #uuid "a47ae42e-bd84-5443-99a9-950e57cfec8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324997} {:answer/id #uuid "998ef4c0-af14-508a-a1da-ca186a2b247c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324998}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a47ae42e-bd84-5443-99a9-950e57cfec8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324997} :answer-field/id #uuid "17f3e912-6da0-531b-8181-a0d140b69fa0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324993}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2e963b65-e179-5879-8768-2b66ce546e2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-93971" :question/problem "The linear form $f(x)$ is defined as $f(x)=ax,$ where $a=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 3 & -4\\end{aligned}].$  Evaluate the function when $x=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Substituting $x=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =ax \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 3 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =(-5)\\cdot 4+3\\cdot 6+(-4)\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =-20+18+8 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186324999 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7083d465-9871-59ca-97fa-583e740e961f" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Bilinear Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d36006ea-a449-577f-8c90-efb65c53cfc2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325001} {:answer/id #uuid "8ad2c848-10b7-57d6-b841-b844960b8452" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325002} {:answer/id #uuid "cd46268c-0b90-5f24-903d-860708d76edd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325003} {:answer/id #uuid "5f30f564-0ec0-5df8-9e92-2e9e6962bceb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325004} {:answer/id #uuid "dfbe5adf-1b2d-5915-8658-56a1f0c08017" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325005}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dfbe5adf-1b2d-5915-8658-56a1f0c08017" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325005} :answer-field/id #uuid "044b55a6-b2ec-5e29-b395-ef488ab23162" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325000}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e7b6530b-3a2a-5822-baf0-f430f46defa6" :question/math-academy-id "q-93976" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nGiven the matrix $A$ above, evaluate the bilinear form $B(x,y)={x}^{T}\\,Ay$ when $x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Substituting $x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],$ we obtain  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & ={x}^{T}\\,Ay \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186325006 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7083d465-9871-59ca-97fa-583e740e961f" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Bilinear Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7f85153-ab0e-5711-8750-010d4b4ecf98" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325008} {:answer/id #uuid "3f664f77-f8fe-56d9-a374-1e35e389f2e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325009} {:answer/id #uuid "33c900c1-4ab0-5488-a7ac-76f649ae3d4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325010} {:answer/id #uuid "bf3776ba-6916-520d-af98-d5accc498124" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325011} {:answer/id #uuid "811e68ab-4958-5d37-a487-b99a7cd5352e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325012}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f664f77-f8fe-56d9-a374-1e35e389f2e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325009} :answer-field/id #uuid "dfb10a91-c247-5a46-841c-21e8a07f1900" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325007}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9015bfef-988b-5059-ae3c-b64198749386" :question/math-academy-id "q-93977" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,-2 & 4 \\\\ \\,2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nGiven the matrix $A$ above, evaluate the bilinear form $B(x,y)={x}^{T}\\,Ay$ when $x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Substituting $x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],$ we obtain   \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & ={x}^{T}\\,Ay \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 9\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =28.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186325013 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7083d465-9871-59ca-97fa-583e740e961f" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Bilinear Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e535bbe9-a2ef-56af-95a6-776ce09c5c49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325015} {:answer/id #uuid "becf0d5f-85cd-5974-9d9b-ec2f7a7e3c3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325016} {:answer/id #uuid "1eff6a69-a0d0-5c3b-9b87-234f92543203" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325017} {:answer/id #uuid "674014d7-02a8-5bab-95bf-062c4a27a3c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325018} {:answer/id #uuid "43519f53-0b98-502a-8d69-116ad9444328" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325019}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43519f53-0b98-502a-8d69-116ad9444328" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325019} :answer-field/id #uuid "44b6b4d3-b63a-57b0-80ce-016894df75d2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325014}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "89f0af3e-6ee2-57cd-b64e-9c8bc1644265" :question/math-academy-id "q-93981" :question/problem "Consider the bilinear form $B(x,y),$ given by \n\n$$\nB(x,y)=2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-4{x}_{2}{y}_{3}+{x}_{3}{y}_{1}-3{x}_{3}{y}_{2}.\n$$\n\n \n\nEvaluate $B(x,y)$ when $x=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "We are given that \n\n$\\,$ $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,y=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nSubstituting these into the bilinear expression, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & =2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-4{x}_{2}{y}_{3}+{x}_{3}{y}_{1}-3{x}_{3}{y}_{2} \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-2)\\cdot 0-4\\cdot 2\\cdot 3+(-1)\\cdot 1-3\\cdot (-1)\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =0-24-1-0 \\\\  & =-25.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186325020 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55277d69-eedc-5c5c-883a-083746e00947" :knowledge-point/title "Writing Down a Bilinear Form Given Its Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49917064-5446-58fa-8e62-a99b5448026e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325022} {:answer/id #uuid "fa0802e8-13b1-5442-bc40-0336d7a2b0c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325023} {:answer/id #uuid "a4967a58-4e66-5c6a-a509-e3bb01b5d258" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325024} {:answer/id #uuid "90960a40-6850-5afd-8e59-1130a341ede1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}-3{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325025} {:answer/id #uuid "d740e8f9-1fdc-578d-a4a1-5f49f3308c72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325026}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d740e8f9-1fdc-578d-a4a1-5f49f3308c72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325026} :answer-field/id #uuid "5988e00c-0c81-5370-9fe9-fc6efd7e3c03" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325021}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e4aa981a-46cc-5351-93da-92c0a2d35b7c" :question/math-academy-id "q-93983" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following represents the corresponding bilinear form ${x}^{T}\\,Ay$ in terms of the components of $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ${a}_{ij}$ of $A$ corresponds to the term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{y}_{j}$ in the expression of the bilinear form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ay & =2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+1{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2} \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a bilinear form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ay & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2{y}_{1}+3{y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+2{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{1}(2{y}_{1}+3{y}_{2})+{x}_{2}({y}_{1}+2{y}_{2}) \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186325027 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55277d69-eedc-5c5c-883a-083746e00947" :knowledge-point/title "Writing Down a Bilinear Form Given Its Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f8d0d9b-66d9-5a6d-9095-0d16d8f9c3bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325029} {:answer/id #uuid "80582d9e-7de8-564e-ab04-48bbf6ee621b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325030} {:answer/id #uuid "66610271-59dd-5bc6-9d1b-aabfb252655d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}-{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325031} {:answer/id #uuid "adade753-5dca-5a04-8b86-89d719cd22cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325032} {:answer/id #uuid "f885d499-29c6-5569-a75c-7665c1b88424" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325033}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f885d499-29c6-5569-a75c-7665c1b88424" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325033} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9079b28-9010-5563-942f-a9e488144d25" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325028}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e69a62e6-eb74-5a0d-a68c-947d87d324da" :question/math-academy-id "q-93984" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following represents the corresponding bilinear form ${x}^{T}\\,Ay$ in terms of the components of $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ${a}_{ij}$ of $A$ corresponds to the term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{y}_{j}$ in the expression of the bilinear form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ay & =(-2){x}_{1}{y}_{1}+1{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+(-1){x}_{2}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2} \\\\  & =-2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a bilinear form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ay & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2{y}_{1}+{y}_{2} \\\\ -{y}_{1}+3{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{1}(-2{y}_{1}+{y}_{2})+{x}_{2}(-{y}_{1}+3{y}_{2}) \\\\  & =-2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186325034 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55277d69-eedc-5c5c-883a-083746e00947" :knowledge-point/title "Writing Down a Bilinear Form Given Its Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21553c69-f8fd-5794-ab18-6e8d6e7f32c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{1}{y}_{1}-{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-3{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325036} {:answer/id #uuid "28f8b3f4-789a-581b-aa89-f64d171295d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}-{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325037} {:answer/id #uuid "5f334a45-0edf-5832-ad38-444ecdf017b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{1}{y}_{1}-2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325038} {:answer/id #uuid "b902301c-bf0c-5515-b9c5-636534cf3aa6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{x}_{1}{y}_{1}-2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325039} {:answer/id #uuid "837022f6-2c66-5448-9e64-2eb09916d725" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{1}{y}_{1}-2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-3{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325040}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f334a45-0edf-5832-ad38-444ecdf017b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{1}{y}_{1}-2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325038} :answer-field/id #uuid "92e76ece-1343-51fc-9cfc-e42a9b64855d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325035}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0d09b6ad-836a-578f-b702-7edb413d5deb" :question/math-academy-id "q-93995" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\,\\,-2 \\\\ \\,\\,-1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following represents the corresponding bilinear form ${x}^{T}\\,Ay$ in terms of the components of $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ${a}_{ij}$ of $A$ corresponds to the term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{y}_{j}$ in the expression of the bilinear form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ay & =1{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+(-2){x}_{1}{y}_{2}+(-1){x}_{2}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{1}{y}_{1}-2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a bilinear form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ay & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & \\,\\,-2 \\\\ \\,\\,-1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}-2{y}_{2} \\\\ -{y}_{1}+3{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{1}({y}_{1}-2{y}_{2})+{x}_{2}(-{y}_{1}+3{y}_{2}) \\\\  & ={x}_{1}{y}_{1}-2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186325041 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55277d69-eedc-5c5c-883a-083746e00947" :knowledge-point/title "Writing Down a Bilinear Form Given Its Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "61cdf0d9-6cf6-56e2-8c76-96eccf6d41c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325043} {:answer/id #uuid "135513f5-0dde-5018-a4d6-3acd03527453" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}-2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325044} {:answer/id #uuid "365f0af1-3684-5d62-9e7c-388a8b5a1ac6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325045} {:answer/id #uuid "ed4833db-ac66-5b36-ac3d-a637a1c8ef40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325046} {:answer/id #uuid "6721e169-08ad-5727-9d9c-89daaf3879db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}-2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325047}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "61cdf0d9-6cf6-56e2-8c76-96eccf6d41c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325043} :answer-field/id #uuid "745d7c33-e5cf-5685-8736-ed6230997889" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325042}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8734aa64-3237-5cf6-ac90-57ea8f324483" :question/math-academy-id "q-93996" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following represents the corresponding bilinear form ${x}^{T}\\,Ay$ in terms of the components of $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ${a}_{ij}$ of $A$ corresponds to the term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{y}_{j}$ in the expression of the bilinear form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ay & =(-2){x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2} \\\\  & =-2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a bilinear form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ay & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2{y}_{1}+2{y}_{2} \\\\ 2{y}_{1}+3{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{1}(-2{y}_{1}+2{y}_{2})+{x}_{2}(2{y}_{1}+3{y}_{2}) \\\\  & =-2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162541 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f60cd05d-e4af-5bf1-8827-cab48da934f1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Bilinear Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85a81cae-2e28-5951-ba79-203ce68a2de1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160879} {:answer/id #uuid "b0b2fc95-c847-5875-8bd8-75e17ef55ceb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160880} {:answer/id #uuid "c6a0e28d-4f6c-5279-87f8-9d357bdecbdc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160881} {:answer/id #uuid "23dc65e4-c125-5a43-8f2d-4b4d68f73f21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160882} {:answer/id #uuid "6179d155-9120-5995-9d4a-73799db9674a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160883}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b0b2fc95-c847-5875-8bd8-75e17ef55ceb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160880} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6214574-4200-561c-a3a8-32986bbb557b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160878}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2cfb9520-59d9-5ad8-a887-b4fdde98c9f4" :question/math-academy-id "q-94040" :question/problem "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & \\,\\,-2 \\\\ 0 & b\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe matrix of the bilinear form $B(x,y)={x}_{1}{y}_{1}-2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}$ is given above. What is the value of $a+b?$" :question/worked-solution "Each term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{y}_{j}$ in the expression of the bilinear form corresponds to the entry ${a}_{ij}$ of the matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & ={x}_{1}{y}_{1}-2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2} \\\\  & =1{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+(-2){x}_{1}{y}_{2} \\\\  & +\\,0{x}_{2}{y}_{1}\\,+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, the corresponding matrix of the bilinear form is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\,\\,-2 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=1$ and $b=2.$ Finally, \n\n$$\na+b=1+2=3.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186325048 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f60cd05d-e4af-5bf1-8827-cab48da934f1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Bilinear Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "66a904bf-0bdc-5d0a-ad06-9f65d13fd33e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325050} {:answer/id #uuid "080b18b8-0cea-5232-99b4-a2dc77b6066d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325051} {:answer/id #uuid "a86e4775-f972-521e-ac48-eb785de79a57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325052} {:answer/id #uuid "6cd59d82-e13f-5196-9ba6-014d58e82f97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325053} {:answer/id #uuid "eeada83d-f6c7-5b9b-8a7f-8b149dfe0853" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325054}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a86e4775-f972-521e-ac48-eb785de79a57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325052} :answer-field/id #uuid "81444873-a47a-5290-8a30-9dd644ae0060" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325049}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "65b5b85d-2ec2-564b-bc86-64c332e5c020" :question/math-academy-id "q-94045" :question/problem "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ -5 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe matrix of the bilinear form $B(x,y)=-4{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-5{x}_{2}{y}_{1}-2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}$ is given above. What is the value of $a+b?$" :question/worked-solution "Each term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{y}_{j}$ in the expression of the bilinear form corresponds to the entry ${a}_{ij}$ of the matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & =-4{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-5{x}_{2}{y}_{1}-2{x}_{2}{y}_{2} \\\\  & =(-4){x}_{1}{y}_{1}+\\,\\,3{x}_{1}{y}_{2} \\\\  & +\\,(-5){x}_{2}{y}_{1}\\,+(-2){x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nThen, the corresponding matrix of the bilinear form is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=-4$ and $b=3.$ Finally, \n\n$$\na+b=-4+3=-1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186325055 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f60cd05d-e4af-5bf1-8827-cab48da934f1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Bilinear Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "77f9b536-bc48-5eec-9d4f-5d87488ee4cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325057} {:answer/id #uuid "91ca4739-e393-5b22-bf27-cda36f488440" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325058} {:answer/id #uuid "569dd683-1adc-5ada-a646-5831c23e6ea1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325059} {:answer/id #uuid "2035ff74-3a6b-5692-98ec-e33828c81285" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325060} {:answer/id #uuid "d9956eba-7d0b-5e64-9261-f8bd4f417b46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/